WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.416
A collection plan translates the requirement into source priorities and lawful search activities.

00:00:05.416 --> 00:00:08.687
Break the main question into smaller information needs.

00:00:08.687 --> 00:00:13.186
For each need, identify likely source categories, expected evidence, collection order,

00:00:13.186 --> 00:00:15.639
time budget, and a clear owner.

00:00:15.639 --> 00:00:18.911
Prioritize sources by relevance, reliability, access, and cost.

00:00:18.911 --> 00:00:23.409
Official records or direct technical documentation may answer some questions efficiently.

00:00:23.409 --> 00:00:25.862
News, social sources, forums, imagery, maps,

00:00:25.862 --> 00:00:30.769
and archives may provide leads or context but often require more validation.

00:00:30.769 --> 00:00:34.041
Develop search concepts rather than one rigid query.

00:00:34.041 --> 00:00:36.494
Record key names, dates, products, locations,

00:00:36.494 --> 00:00:40.175
and public identifiers that are necessary to the requirement.

00:00:40.175 --> 00:00:43.855
Plan how terms may vary across languages or time.

00:00:43.855 --> 00:00:49.171
Search strategy should remain transparent and reproducible rather than relying on unexplained intuition.

00:00:49.171 --> 00:00:52.442
Build legal and ethical constraints into the plan.

00:00:52.442 --> 00:00:55.714
Document approved public access, organizational policy, privacy boundaries,

00:00:55.714 --> 00:00:57.759
handling requirements, and escalation points.

00:00:57.759 --> 00:01:03.075
Do not plan to bypass access controls, use deceptive identities, obtain stolen credentials,

00:01:03.075 --> 00:01:06.346
or enter spaces that are not legitimately available.

00:01:06.346 --> 00:01:07.164
Avoid overcollection.

00:01:07.164 --> 00:01:11.253
More data can increase false associations, privacy exposure, storage burden,

00:01:11.253 --> 00:01:12.480
and analytical noise.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.160
Collect the minimum material needed to evaluate the requirement.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:21.885
Sensitive personal information should not be gathered merely because it appears in a result.

00:01:21.885 --> 00:01:22.703
Include contingencies.

00:01:22.703 --> 00:01:27.201
A source may disappear, conflict with another record, or prove unreliable.

00:01:27.201 --> 00:01:32.517
Identify alternatives and specify when to pause for legal, privacy, or supervisory review.

00:01:32.517 --> 00:01:39.060
A good collection plan focuses effort while leaving room to adapt when evidence changes the direction.
